<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
    <!--
        Vulnerability Waiver Registry
        ==============================
        Purpose: record auditable, time-bounded waivers for pre-existing High findings that
        cannot be fixed immediately. Criticals may NOT be waived — they must be fixed,
        upgraded, or escalated with maintainer sign-off recorded in the pull request.

        Required fields in every <suppress> entry (inside <notes>):
          owner:   GitHub username or team name responsible for remediation
          reason:  justification for the waiver (why it cannot be fixed right now)
          expires: yyyy-MM-dd — 90 days from triage date; must be renewed or fixed before expiry

        POLICY:
          • Any entry missing an 'expires:' line causes the build to fail.
          • Any entry whose 'expires:' date is today or in the past causes the build to fail.
          • Use GAV coordinates (not just CVE) for transitive-only findings with no direct
            upgrade path, so unrelated future findings are not silently suppressed.
          • Triage SLA: findings must be waived, fixed, or escalated within 5 working days
            of discovery.

        Known limitation (npm):
          npm 6 (pinned in package.json / build.gradle) does not support the 'overrides'
          field.  Transitive npm vulnerabilities that cannot be resolved without an npm
          version bump are recorded here and deferred to the package-manager uplift story.
          CI runs 'npm audit --audit-level=high' to surface these findings; the exit code
          is soft-suppressed with documentation until the npm uplift lands.

        Self-hosted fork operators:
          Set the NVD_API_KEY environment variable to your own key
          (https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/request-an-api-key) for full NVD update
          throughput.  The first run downloads the full NVD dataset (~200 MB) and can
          take 10-20 minutes; subsequent runs use the cached data directory.

        Initial triage: 2026-07-30
        All entries below expire 90 days from triage date: 2026-10-28.
    -->

    <!-- =====================================================================
         jQuery 1.4.4 — src/main/webapp/js/jquery/jquery-1.4.4.js
         Rationale: served only from legacy GSP pages; the React SPA bundles
         its own modern jQuery-free dependencies.  Upgrade blocked on the
         GSP-to-React migration (Phase 5 of the modernisation roadmap, ~2028).
         Attack surface: authenticated internal users only; no public exposure.
         Fix target: remove when GSP pages are migrated (Phase 5).
         ===================================================================== -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
owner: security-team
reason: jQuery 1.4.4 prototype pollution ($.extend). File used only in legacy GSP pages
        (not the React SPA). Upgrade blocked on Phase 5 GSP-to-React migration.
        Deployment topology limits exposure to authenticated, internal-network users.
expires: 2026-10-28
        ]]></notes>
        <filePath regex="true">.*jquery-1\.4\.4\.js</filePath>
        <cve>CVE-2019-11358</cve>
    </suppress>

